//@version=5
// V17 -- the one engineered feature that survived. A Donchian breakout pays when, and only when,
// it is ALSO above the last completed regular-session high.
//
// ================================ WHAT THIS ADDS ================================
// The base is V11, re-measured rather than inherited: Donchian 55 entry / 20 exit, ADX(14) >= 25,
// stop 2.5 x ATR(20), one unit, no take profit, LONG, market order at the next open, NQ 15-minute.
// V17 adds one filter -- **the signal bar's close must be at or above the high of the last
// completed 09:30-16:00 New York session.**
//
//   block      filter   trades   net R   R/trade      PF    win%   Sharpe   maxDD   R/DD
//   research   off         333   +55.9   +0.1680   1.328   38.14%   1.08     16.4R   3.41
//   research   ON          238   +63.0   +0.2649   1.566   42.02%   1.38     11.6R   5.46
//   LOCKED     off         174   +23.6   +0.1356   1.308   37.93%   1.05     14.3R   1.65
//   LOCKED     ON          129   +41.2   +0.3191   1.780   43.41%   1.55      9.0R   4.56
//
// Profit factor 1.31 -> 1.78 and Sharpe 1.05 -> 1.55 out of sample, on 26% fewer trades and 37%
// less drawdown. **Sharpe here is computed over EVERY trading day in the block, zero-filled on days
// that did not trade** -- over traded days only, a filter is paid for trading less, and this one
// would look far better than it is.
//
// ================================ WHY THIS ONE AND NOT THE OTHERS ================================
// **THE POOL AS A WHOLE FOUND NOTHING.** 21 engineered features x 6 levels x 2 directions = 285
// scorable conditions. 16 beat a random filter of the same selectivity on Sharpe at p <= 0.05
// against **14.2 expected by chance**; on net R only 7 passed against 14.2 expected, which is worse
// than chance. Read that before reading anything below.
//
// This condition was carried on SHAPE, not rank -- it was not even the best cell. It is the only
// feature in the pool whose entire ladder is sign-consistent in both directions on research:
//
//   below the session high   -2.0N: -0.103   -0.5N: -0.060   0.0: -0.046   +0.5N: -0.040  R/trade
//   above the session high   -0.5N: +0.233    0.0: +0.265   +0.5N: +0.251   +1.5N: +0.364  R/trade
//
// Every rung of one side loses and every rung of the other wins. **And the gradient replicated out
// of sample**, which is the part a lucky cell cannot do:
//
//   LOCKED           <= level              >= level
//   -2.0N       -0.153 R/trade        +0.199 R/trade
//   -0.5N       +0.050               +0.195
//    0.0        +0.017               +0.319      <- shipped
//   +0.5N       +0.057               +0.295
//   +1.5N       +0.166               +0.244
//
// The level shipped is **0** and not the +1.5N that scores best on research: zero is the boundary
// the feature already has, needs no parameter, and keeps 49 more trades.
//
// ================================ WHAT IT IS NOT ================================
// It is not the daily trend, and it is not the prior close. Both were in the same pool with the
// same controls and neither works:
//
//   condition                          trades   R/trade      PF   Sharpe        p
//   close >= last session HIGH            238   +0.2649   1.566     1.38   0.0067   <- this
//   close >= last session CLOSE           322   +0.1809   1.354     1.13   0.1500
//   daily ADX >= 15                       301   +0.1850   1.367     1.12   0.2267
//   daily close > EMA200                  327   +0.1530   1.297     0.99   0.9900
//   daily EMA20 > EMA50                   277   +0.1372   1.265     0.81   0.9933
//   daily uptrend AND daily ADX > 20      176   +0.1771   1.337     0.75   0.9467
//   daily +DI > -DI                       234   +0.1028   1.199     0.56   1.0000
//
// A LEVEL, not a trend, and specifically the HIGH. The reading is that a 55-bar channel break on 15
// minutes and a break of yesterday's session high are two different levels agreeing, and the trade
// is worth taking when they do.
//
// ================================ THE CONTROL, WHICH THE BASE FAILS ================================
// Random entries with the same side, geometry and minute-of-day mix, 2,000 draws:
//
//                     research            LOCKED
//   base only      p = 0.0135          p = 0.2130    <- the base does NOT clear its control here
//   + this filter  p = 0.0055          p = 0.0140    (x2 = 0.0280 for the two conditions read)
//
// The filter is what makes the strategy clear a control it otherwise fails out of sample. Bootstrap
// on the locked daily series: P(mean daily R <= 0) = **0.0234**. Drop a random 10% of days and the
// locked Sharpe p5 is 1.18, median 1.57.
//
// **AND THE HONEST CEILING ON THAT NUMBER:** 285 conditions were searched on research. Bonferroni
// over the whole search puts 0.014 x 285 well past 1, so the p-value is not the evidence -- the
// evidence is that the GRADIENT, not just the cell, reproduced on a block it was not chosen on.
// Treat it as one replication, not as a settled result.
//
// ================================ THE RUNNER-UP, WHICH SHIPS OFF ================================
// `close - channel <= 0.1 x ATR` -- the rule against chasing a break that has already run -- was
// the other condition strong enough on research to spend a holdout read on: four consecutive rungs
// at p 0.003-0.037 with the opposite direction uniformly worse.
//
//   research   293 trades  +0.2544 R/trade  PF 1.536  Sharpe 1.48   control p 0.0005
//   LOCKED     155 trades  +0.1522 R/trade  PF 1.374  Sharpe 1.20   control p 0.1725   <- fails
//
// It is available as an input and defaults OFF. Turning it on WITH the shipped filter gives the
// best numbers in the whole study -- locked 109 trades, +0.3961 R/trade, PF 2.068, Sharpe 1.71,
// control p 0.0040 -- but its own solo read failed, so its marginal contribution is not
// established and 109 trades is thin. That combination is a measurement, not a recommendation.
//
// ================================ PARITY ================================
// Two things had to match, not one. The session-high series the script builds on its own bars is
// **identical to the tick** to the research construction (which aggregates 1-minute bars and maps
// each intraday bar to the last session closing strictly before it), and the CONDITION agrees on
// **100.0000%** of bars. The order model then matches the engine at 100% signal match, 100%
// exit-bar match and correlation 1.0000, filter on and off, on both blocks.
// A leakage assertion is part of the harness: zero bars map to a session that had not closed.
//
// ================================ COSTS ================================
// MNQ, itemised: broker + exchange + clearing + NFA per side, half a one-tick spread, and slippage
// scaled by the bar's true range against the series median, doubled outside 09:30-16:00, with an
// extra tick on a stop fill.
// ==========================================================================================

strategy("V17 Donchian 55 + prior session high", overlay = true, pyramiding = 0,
     default_qty_type = strategy.fixed, default_qty_value = 1,
     initial_capital = 100000, calc_on_every_tick = false, process_orders_on_close = false,
     commission_type = strategy.commission.cash_per_order, commission_value = 0.72, slippage = 2)

// ===================== STRATEGY TESTER PROPERTIES =====================
//   Script execution   ON BAR CLOSE only -- see docs/ib/STUDY_TICK_RECALC.md.
//   Slippage           2 ticks. Entry is a market order and the exit is a stop; both cross.
//   Leverage Infinity  stops silent order rejection; then read DOLLAR drawdown, not %.
//   Timeframe          15 minutes. The base was compared at 15m and 30m and 15m won on both blocks.
// ======================================================================

gE       = "Entry"
donLen   = input.int(55, "Donchian breakout length", minval = 2, group = gE)
adxMin   = input.float(25, "ADX(14) floor", minval = 0, step = 1, group = gE,
     tooltip="25, not 15. Reproduced independently here: without it the base falls from +0.1680 to +0.0574 R/trade on research and from +0.1356 to +0.1091 on locked.")
usePdh   = input.bool(true, "Require close >= last session high", group = gE,
     tooltip="The engineered filter. Locked: profit factor 1.308 -> 1.780, Sharpe 1.05 -> 1.55, drawdown 14.3R -> 9.0R, and it is what makes the strategy clear a matched control it otherwise fails out of sample.")
pdhSess  = input.session("0930-1600", "Session whose high is used, New York", group = gE)
useChase = input.bool(false, "Also require the break to be un-extended", group = gE,
     tooltip="close - channel <= 0.1 x ATR, the rule against chasing. Research control p 0.0005, LOCKED control p 0.1725 -- it failed its own holdout read, so it ships off. With the filter above it gives locked PF 2.068 and Sharpe 1.71 on 109 trades, which is a measurement, not a recommendation.")
chaseMax = input.float(0.1, "  maximum extension, x ATR", step = 0.05, group = gE)

gX       = "Exit"
atrLen   = input.int(20, "ATR length", minval = 2, group = gX,
     tooltip="ATR here is ema(TR, n), NOT ta.atr -- ta.atr is Wilder's RMA and a different series. Every level in this script is sized in the EMA form because the research layer is.")
stopMult = input.float(2.5, "ATR stop multiple", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = gX)
exitCh   = input.int(20, "Donchian exit channel", minval = 2, group = gX)
qty      = input.int(1, "Contracts", minval = 1, group = gX)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------- series
atrN   = ta.ema(ta.tr(true), atrLen)
// ENTRY channel excludes the current bar so a break is possible.
entHi  = ta.highest(high, donLen)[1]
// EXIT channel takes NO [1]: the order is placed at this bar's close and is live on the next, so
// this is the window the engine reads on the bar it fires.
exLo   = ta.lowest(low, exitCh)
[_pdi, _mdi, adxVal] = ta.dmi(14, 14)      // returns [+DI, -DI, ADX] IN THAT ORDER

// THE LAST COMPLETED SESSION HIGH, accumulated on this chart's own bars and frozen when the session
// ends. `request.security` on a daily bar would give the 24-hour futures high, which is a different
// number; this tracks the 09:30-16:00 New York session the research uses, and it was verified
// identical to the tick against that construction.
// BARE `hour`/`minute` ARE EXCHANGE TIME IN PINE -- Chicago for CME -- so the session is resolved
// with an explicit timezone.
inRTH  = not na(time(timeframe.period, pdhSess, "America/New_York"))
var float curHi  = na
var float lastHi = na
if barstate.isconfirmed
    if inRTH and not inRTH[1]
        curHi := high
    else if inRTH
        curHi := na(curHi) ? high : math.max(curHi, high)
    if not inRTH and inRTH[1] and not na(curHi)
        lastHi := curHi

ready   = not na(atrN) and atrN > 0
pdhOk   = not usePdh or (not na(lastHi) and close >= lastHi)
chaseOk = not useChase or (not na(entHi) and close - entHi <= chaseMax * atrN)
sigL    = ready and pdhOk and chaseOk and (not na(adxVal) and adxVal >= adxMin)
     and not na(entHi) and high > entHi

// ----------------------------------------------------------------- state
var float sigAtr    = na     // ATR FROZEN AT THE SIGNAL BAR; the stop distance reads this all trade
var int   lastCnt   = 0
var int   closedBar = na

// EVERY var-STATE BLOCK IS GUARDED, AND SO IS THE EXIT CALL -- docs/ib/STUDY_TICK_RECALC.md.
if barstate.isconfirmed and strategy.position_size == 0 and lastCnt > 0
    sigAtr := na
    lastCnt := 0
    closedBar := bar_index

if barstate.isconfirmed and strategy.opentrades > lastCnt
    lastCnt := strategy.opentrades

// A position cannot re-arm on the bar it closed on: the engine's lock requires the next signal to
// be strictly after the exit bar, and Pine is already flat at that bar's close.
flat = strategy.position_size == 0 and (na(closedBar) or bar_index > closedBar)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------- entry, bracket riding with it
// THE EXIT MUST BE LIVE ON THE ENTRY BAR -- the engine starts its walk at the fill bar, so a
// bracket that waits for the next bar leaves the first bar of every trade uncovered.
// `stop` and `loss` together give exactly max(ATR stop, channel): Pine takes whichever produces the
// SMALLER LOSS, which for a long is the HIGHER of the two prices. Two separate orders race.
lvlL = math.min(exLo, close)      // a sell stop cannot rest above the market

if barstate.isconfirmed and flat and sigL
    sigAtr := atrN
    strategy.entry("L", strategy.long, qty = qty)
    strategy.exit("x", from_entry = "L", stop = lvlL,
         loss = int(math.max(1, math.round(stopMult * atrN / syminfo.mintick))))

// ----------------------------------------------------------------- exit, re-priced each bar
if barstate.isconfirmed and strategy.position_size != 0 and lastCnt > 0 and not na(sigAtr)
    strategy.exit("x", from_entry = "L", stop = lvlL,
         loss = int(math.max(1, math.round(stopMult * sigAtr / syminfo.mintick))))

// ----------------------------------------------------------------- plots
plot(entHi, "Donchian 55 high", color = color.new(color.teal, 30))
plot(lastHi, "Last session high", color = color.new(color.orange, 0), linewidth = 2,
     style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(strategy.position_size > 0 ? lvlL : na, "Working stop", color = color.fuchsia,
     style = plot.style_linebr)
bgcolor(usePdh and not na(lastHi) and close >= lastHi ? color.new(color.teal, 95) : na,
     title = "above last session high")

onTf = timeframe.period == "15"
var table hud = table.new(position.top_right, 1, 4, border_width = 1)
if barstate.islast
    table.cell(hud, 0, 0, "V17 - locked PF 1.78, Sharpe 1.55, maxDD 9.0R, control p 0.014",
         text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.teal, 20))
    table.cell(hud, 0, 1, onTf ? "15m chart" : "NOT 15m - the base was chosen at 15m",
         text_color = color.white, bgcolor = onTf ? color.new(color.teal, 45) : color.red)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 2, usePdh ? "Session-high filter ON - PF 1.31 -> 1.78 out of sample" : "Filter OFF - this is the bare base, control p 0.213 on locked",
         text_color = color.white, bgcolor = usePdh ? color.new(color.teal, 45) : color.new(color.orange, 20))
    table.cell(hud, 0, 3, "The POOL was null: 16 of 285 passed, 14.2 expected. One replication, not a settled result.",
         text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.red, 20))
